WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:04.233
When people hear 'full stack developer,' they imagine deeply complex code.

2
00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:07.333
Here is what most apps actually do.

3
00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:11.867
They take input from a user. Store it. Retrieve it. Show it to someone else.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.900
That is it. That is most of the internet.

5
00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:18.933
Instagram? Users post images. Images get stored. Other users see them.

6
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:23.000
Uber? A rider requests. A driver is matched. Both see a map update.

7
00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:26.533
WhatsApp? Someone types. Words travel. Another person reads them.

8
00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:30.833
The complexity is not in the idea — it is in scale, speed, and reliability.

9
00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:34.600
Full stack developers master both sides of the equation.

10
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:38.167
Frontend is the face. Backend is the brain.

11
00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:41.433
Together, they build every app you use today.

12
00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:45.233
Build real applications at 0xverse Academy.

